"""Reference solution for ``foreach_max`` (aten::_foreach_max).

Declared entrypoint of the existing ``--override foreach_max:<file>:run``
protocol.  It is called with the target list of tensors exactly as the tests and
the benchmark call ``flag_gems.foreach_max``, and it returns one
zero-dimensional maximum per input tensor, preserving each input's dtype and
device (frozen Definition: ``Tensor[] self -> Tensor[]``, no mutation, no
returned alias).

The reduction is the native ATen op, which is also the oracle the accuracy
cases compare against.  It never imports or calls the FlagGems candidate export,
so it cannot re-enter the operator under validation.
"""

import torch


def run(tensors):
    return torch.ops.aten._foreach_max(tensors)
